  "footnotes": [
    "[a] A solution of fluoroiodomethane (1); 0.10 M in THF); flow rate: 4.0 mL min^-1) and a solution of MeLi (Br free; 0.20 M in Et2O; flow rate: 4.0 mL min^-1) or LDA (0.42 M in THF; flow rate: 1.0 mL min^-1) were introduced to M1 by syringe pumps. The resulting solution was passed through R1 (tR1 = 0.013 s, T = -60 °C (4j-o); tR1 = 0.082 s, T = -40 °C (6d and 6e), -60 °C (6f)) and was mixed with a solution of electrophiles (0.30 M in THF; flow rate: 4.0 mL min^-1) in M2. The resulting solution was passed through R2 (tR2 = 7.85 s, T = -60 °C (4j-o); tR2 = 20.94 s, T = -40 °C ((6d and 6e), -60 °C (6f)).",
    "[b] Yield was determined by GC analysis using dodecane as an internal standard.",
    "[c] Yields were determined by 1H NMR analysis using dibromomethane as an internal standard."
  ],
  "notes": "An unlabelled column for the product number designations (4j, 4k, etc.) was assigned the header 'Label'. Based on the reaction reagents, MeLi effects I-Li exchange of fluoroiodomethane to form fluoromethyllithium (2) which attacks Weinreb amides and ketones. LDA deprotonates fluoroiodomethane to form fluoroiodomethyllithium (3), which reacts with ketones followed by intramolecular cyclization (Darzens-type reaction) to yield fluoroepoxides.",
  "_source_paper": "Nagaki_2020_CHLiIF",
